# Structure Rules

## Project layout

```
storycraft-kit/                    # BOXELS/storycraft-kit (private)
├── crates/
│   ├── core/                      # storycraft-core: paths, flags, apps, clients, doctor, recipe, engine, verify, pack, bug
│   │   ├── src/                   # one module per concern; pack/ holds the .ico and .icns writers
│   │   └── tests/it/              # end-to-end recipe runs against fake app CLIs
│   ├── sc/                        # `sc` CLI binary
│   └── mcp/                       # `storycraft-mcp` stdio server binary
├── recipes/                       # Declarative multi-app workflows (*.yaml) + presets/
│   └── presets/                   # Looks and output specs: youtube-thumbnail.yaml, icon-set.yaml, icon-targets.yaml
├── templates/                     # Source documents recipes open (monogram icon .vectorcraft, thumbnail .psd)
├── apps/                          # Per-app knowledge: command-ID maps per version (photocraft/0.23.json …)
├── tests/live/                    # opt-in runs against real apps on the Mac (not yet written)
├── mac/                           # Quick Action / Shortcuts, later the optional desktop app
├── docs/                          # Agent-facing reference docs (see documentation.mdc)
├── notes/contributions.md         # Log of issues/PRs filed upstream (newest first)
├── .cursor/{rules,skills,agents}/ # This rules set, skills, worker subagent
├── .claude/agents/                # Claude Code subagents
└── AGENTS.md
```

## File placement rules

- New workflows are recipes in `recipes/`, not new Rust code. Add code only when a recipe needs a new step type, verifier or packer.
- Templates a recipe opens live in `templates/` with a provenance line in `templates/README.md` (our own work only).
- Per-app command maps go in `apps/<app>/<version>.json`, generated by `sc commands <app> --json`, never hand-written.
- Job outputs never go in the repo (default job root outside it, decision D3).
- Agent/reference documentation goes in `docs/` — see `documentation.mdc`.
- Configuration (`Cargo.toml`, `rust-toolchain.toml`, `rustfmt.toml`) stays in the root.
- Cursor rules live in `.cursor/rules/` as `.mdc` files with YAML frontmatter (`description`, `alwaysApply`, optional `globs`). Plain `.md` files in that folder are ignored by Cursor.
- Cursor skills live in `.cursor/skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md`. Rule = standing instruction; skill = repeatable procedure.
- `AGENTS.md` at the root is a thin pointer for non-Cursor agents. Don't duplicate rule content into it.

## Naming conventions

- Directories and recipe files: kebab-case (`youtube-thumbnail.yaml`).
- Rust: `snake_case.rs` files, `PascalCase` types, `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` constants.
- Job dirs: `<YYYY-MM-DD>-<recipe>-<short-id>/`.
- Outputs: `<AppName>-icons/<platform>/…`, `thumbnail-<variant>.jpg`.

## When creating new files

1. Check whether an existing recipe, verifier, or module can be extended first.
2. Never create a file outside this structure without asking.
3. Propose any new top-level directory before creating it.
4. If a file exceeds ~300 lines, consider splitting it by responsibility.
